# Content and documents

Document is an optional platform-neutral binding owned by `route.dart`. It
merges route-owned metadata and HTML trees, then renders a complete response
without a JavaScript framework.

## Semantic route

```dart
final route =
    AppRoute<NoParams, NoSearch, NoData>().document(
      (_) => const RouteDocument(
        title: 'About',
        body: HtmlElement(
          'article',
          children: <HtmlNode>[
            HtmlElement(
              'h1',
              children: <HtmlNode>[HtmlText('About')],
            ),
          ],
        ),
      ),
    );
```

When a route also has a Flutter page, the server emits readable HTML and
handoff state before Flutter takes over. Completed and pending Query values use
the same explicit serializer contract; see
[Query server handoff](/docs/concepts/query#server-handoff).
The browser handoff, streamed frames, semantic HTML transition, and external
Router navigation use the same DOM implementation in JavaScript and
WebAssembly builds.

## Press

Press turns an MDC directory into an immutable content snapshot.

```dart
final docs = PressDirectory('content/docs', mount: '/docs');
final snapshot = await docs.snapshot();
final page = snapshot.page(<String>['getting-started']);
```

Successful snapshots are atomic and cached. Changed files are reparsed;
unchanged pages retain identity. Drafts, duplicate URLs, invalid frontmatter,
and files changing during a read are handled explicitly.

This website uses Press for the page you are reading and returns its locations
from `lib/prerender.dart`.
